  {
    "episode_id": 76922,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76922.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "You know, that's a very interesting question and one that somewhat shockingly, actually, I'm realizing no one had asked before, and I'm not even sure I've asked myself. I think the assumption amongst most people I've talked to has been that actually the insurrection and the pandemic are divorced, that one is about right-wing extremism and a digital environment that ferments conspiracy theories and sedition, and the other has been about the elements of contagion in the globalized world and the incompetence of the federal government. And I'm not sure anybody's asked me how they intersect. I don't know that I have a great answer for that. I think my thought would be that we would have had this and, you know, imagine a counterfactual where there was no pandemic, but Trump still lost. I still think he would have done the same series of things. I'd be interested for your thoughts on that, though, Scott. I mean, do you think that, how do you think they related?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
