        "text": "People generally believe complex societal events should be explained through distinct, non-overlapping causes.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "It is reasonable to treat political violence and public health crises as analytically separate domains.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker's interlocutors prioritize clear categorical distinctions when interpreting major historical events.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Social narratives around major events often reflect dominant ideological frameworks rather than integrated analysis.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
