  },
  {
    "episode_id": 76922,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76922.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, to me, the two, I mean, I like the way you framed the counterfactual too, whether it have happened even without the pandemic, but it's hard to look away from the amount of disinformation in the system. And the poor leadership that's been on display from the beginning, and you've been very eloquent about that and talking about the president and the failure of leadership, and he just had many more opportunities to demonstrate that. And to look for that fracturing of society, it seemed almost that what most of us think of as a mishandling of the pandemic became an electoral strategy for him. And I guess that's what I wanted to sort of get more of a sense for you, the sort of broader political ecosystem that we're operating in here in which the pandemic has brought to the fore very many ugly things.",
