  {
    "episode_id": 76922,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76922.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "The private sector is pretty good in a lot of this stuff. It just needs to de-risk the investments it has to make. And we've spent, I don't know the exact number, $4 trillion, $5 trillion now of government money on relief and are going to probably spend more. We could take a whole comma off of that and it made it $500 billion. If the President of the United States had said to the 50 biggest companies, here, come take a tour of our printing press. We're literally going to keep this thing running. And it doesn't matter how much it costs, you need to come up with the vaccine distribution and testing and PPE that we need. And we'll pre-pay for it. It would have solved so much. And there was just not that leadership and foresight.",
