    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "really help to tell the truth. We've spent four years lying nonstop, so we shouldn't be surprised that people think that there's a trust gap. And I say we as the royal, we have the federal government. Obviously, there's a lot of people who have been telling the truth. The key actors, the president and his enablers in the last four years have just been lying nonstop. I mean, it's just we're drowning in lies as a democracy. And the most important thing we can do is tell the truth. My constituent, Dr. Walensky, the new incoming head of the CDC wrote an op-ed for the New York Times saying, I will tell the truth even when the news is grim. And that's exactly the right attitude for elected officials to have, just tell people the truth. You had mentioned that trust in science is declining. I'm gonna have to, I made to diverge with you on that. I'm not sure that's true. I actually think trust in science is on the upswing. Science as an institution along with the military tends to rank pretty high in public opinion polls. And I think that's because science by its very definition is one of empirical truth-seeking. And we've seen major scientific figures like Dr. Fauci gain tremendous profile by just being honest. So I'd like to see science double down. And I say that somewhat selfishly as representative from what I would argue is probably the life sciences capital of the world here in right outside Greater Boston. I'd like to see life sciences continue to flourish with the tail winds of this pandemic and their response to it.",
